Source: usability-misc
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Patrick Schleizer <adrelanos@kicksecure.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 13.11.6),
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 config-package-dev
Homepage: https://github.com/Kicksecure/usability-misc
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/Kicksecure/usability-misc
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/Kicksecure/usability-misc.git
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: usability-misc
Architecture: all
Depends: policyrcd-script-zg2, adduser, python3, damngpl,
 helper-scripts (>= 3:35.3-1), dkms, ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: desktop-config-dist (<< 3:13.8-1)
Replaces: gpl-sources-download, scurl, grub-screen-resolution
Description: Misc usability improvements
 A collection of shell wrappers, configuration drop-ins, systemd units
 and desktop defaults for Kicksecure and Whonix.
 .
 CLI tools:
 .
  * scurl - curl wrapper enforcing TLS 1.3 and HTTPS-only
    (--tlsv1.3 --proto =https).
  * scurl-download / curl-download (curlget) - wcurl wrappers,
    scurl-download adds --tlsv1.3.
  * gsudoedit - runs sudoedit with a graphical askpass dialog
    (Wayland-compatible, uses yad).
  * gpl_download_sources - downloads GPL-licensed source code of all
    installed packages via damngpl + apt-get source.
  * ip_unpriv - runs /bin/ip through passwordless sudo for the
    unprivileged "tunnel" user.
  * iptables-save-deterministic - outputs iptables-save with counters
    zeroed and comments stripped for diffable results.
  * repo-add-dist - adds the Kicksecure APT repository and signing key.
  * dist-installer-cli - CLI installer for Kicksecure/Whonix (source
    script; auto-generates the standalone version).
  * virtualbox-send-sysrq - sends SysRq key combinations to a
    VirtualBox VM via VBoxManage.
  * whonix-dev-backup - backs up Kicksecure/Whonix GitHub repos and
    wiki dumps.
  * flameshot.dist - Flameshot wrapper setting Wayland (sway)
    environment variables for compatibility.
  * orca-enable-autostart - removes the OnlyShowIn restriction from
    Orca screen reader autostart.
 .
 sudo configuration (/etc/sudoers.d/):
 .
  * pwfeedback - shows asterisks while typing the sudo password.
  * sudo-lecture-disable - disables the first-run sudo lecture.
  * tunnel_unpriv - commented-out rules to allow unprivileged OpenVPN.
  * user-passwordless - commented-out rule to let the "user" account
    run all commands without a password. Disabled by default.
 .
 GRUB and boot:
 .
  * Sets 1024x768 boot screen resolution via GRUB_GFXPAYLOAD_LINUX.
    /etc/default/grub.d/30_screen_resolution.cfg
    Skipped in Qubes.
  * Adds a GRUB submenu for switching keyboard layouts at boot.
    /etc/grub.d/44_kb_layout
  * Generates GRUB keyboard layouts during package install using
    set-grub-keymap --build-all.
  * Creates Secure Boot MOK key using shim-signed-mok-setup (provided
    by package helper-scripts) during installation.
 .
 Shell environment:
 .
  * Sets VISUAL to featherpad or mousepad if available and unset.
    /etc/profile.d/50_default_editor.sh
  * Prepends /usr/share/usability-misc/xdg-override/ to XDG_DATA_DIRS,
    setting pcmanfm-qt as default file manager.
 .
 Zsh configuration (/etc/zsh/):
 .
  * Ships a complete zsh configuration (prompt, completions, vi-mode
    key bindings, syntax highlighting, auto-suggestions).
  * Does not configure zsh as default shell.
    (That is up to package dist-base-files.)
  * Silences the zsh-newuser-install wizard.
 .
 APT:
 .
  * Speeds up apt-get update by disabling language translations and
    Contents index. /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/30usability-misc
 .
 systemd services and drop-ins:
 .
  * avoid-needless-polkit-agent.service - disables the polkit
    authentication agent in unprivileged user sessions (when
    user-sysmaint-split is installed).
  * check-user-slice-on-shutdown.service - reports hung user processes
    during shutdown.
  * orca-kill-at-shutdown.service - gracefully terminates the Orca
    screen reader at shutdown.
  * console-setup.service.d/30_fix.conf - workaround for a setupcon
    tmpfile race condition (Debian bug #846256).
  * openvpn@openvpn.service.d/50_unpriv.conf - runs OpenVPN as the
    unprivileged "tunnel" user.
  * usbguard*.service.d/ - skip USBGuard services when no PCI USB
    controller is present (virtual machines).
  * Enables systemd-journald-audit.socket (required by apparmor-info
    and apparmor-watch).
    https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1038993
 .
 Kernel modules:
 .
  * Prevents KVM and VirtualBox from conflicting by setting
    enable_virt_at_load=0 for the kvm module.
    /usr/lib/modprobe.d/usability-misc.conf
 .
 DKMS:
 .
  * Lowers parallel compilation jobs to 1 on systems with less than
    2 GB RAM to prevent VM freezes.
    /etc/dkms/framework.conf.d/30_usability-misc.conf
 .
 Desktop integration:
 .
  * On-Screen Keyboard desktop entries for launching/stopping wvkbd.
  * Mousepad configured to open files in new windows instead of tabs
    (gsettings override).
  * XFCE Terminal skeleton config: unlimited scrollback, no
    scroll-on-output. /etc/skel/.config/xfce4/terminal/terminalrc
  * Creates ~/Downloads and ~/Pictures via skeleton placeholders.
 .
 Package postinst actions:
 .
  * Creates the "tunnel" system user for unprivileged OpenVPN.
  * Creates /usr/share/desktop-directories (Bisq workaround).
    https://github.com/bisq-network/bisq/issues/848
  * Adds account "user" to group libvirt and group kvm.
  * Runs update-grub if available.
